1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,420
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:08,425
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,677
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,721
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,352
[Cita] <i>Don't ever show yourself</i>
<i>to me and Karla again!</i>

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,270
PREVIOUSLY

8
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:22,605
I'll press charges
for what you did to my child!

9
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,023
Rot in jail!

10
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:29,529
Maybe we were wrong
to try to rebuild this family.

11
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:31,656
[Audrey] <i>Stay here with Ibyang.</i>

12
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,783
<i>My child and I are going home.</i>

13
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:36,411
[Atoy] <i>Don't leave. I love you and Janine.</i>

14
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:40,040
I thought things were okay
with Aunt Audrey.

15
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:44,085
[Ame] <i>I'm sure Atoy won't leave you.</i>

16
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:45,837
<i>He'll make a compromise.</i>

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,964
Your Brother Emerson is here…

18
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:49,215
um…

19
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:51,676
to take you home.

20
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:54,804
Why are you punishing me?

21
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:57,390
[Audrey] <i>Your daddy is sending</i>
<i>Ibyang home.</i>

22
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:59,434
<i>I just feel bad for her.</i>

23
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:00,643
Don't cry anymore,

24
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,396
because you and Daddy are back together,
and we're complete now.

25
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,774
Then he shouldn't have promised
to adopt Ibyang

26
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:07,650
if he wasn't going to do it.

27
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:12,822
[Ibyang] <i>I won't force myself on someone</i>
<i>who can't choose me.</i>

28
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:15,033
[Atoy] <i>Ibyang left me.</i>

29
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,537
<i>She's upset with me. She's sulking.</i>

30
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:27,170
Godmother…

31
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:30,673
Are they here?

32
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,554
[music fades]

33
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:37,722
Ame!

34
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,933
Come out! [inhales]

35
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:42,560
It's better if you all face each other.

36
00:01:43,853 --> 00:01:45,438
- [Cita] Go ahead.
- [Ame] Oh.

37
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:49,692
[melancholic music playing]

38
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:52,570
Atoy, I'm sorry.

39
00:01:52,654 --> 00:01:55,365
Ibyang doesn't want to see you.

40
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:58,159
That's why she asked to leave.

41
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:00,787
She said she'll give way to your family.

42
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:05,416
Anyway, once I find another job,
I'll leave the shop too.

43
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,128
Hey, what do you mean you're leaving?
Who's leaving?

44
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,879
You still have work with me.

45
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,215
You'll work for me, no one else.

46
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,550
Ame, what's wrong with you?

47
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:15,677
- Okay. Since you said so.
- [Cita chuckles]

48
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,596
Eh, ah-- Where's Ibyang?

49
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,223
- [soft moan]
- [music fades]

50
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:21,224
[clatters]

51
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,392
[Ibyang gasps]

52
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:23,351
[suspicious music playing]

53
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:25,854
Ibya-- Ibyang!

54
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:28,022
Ibyang, come here.

55
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,899
Let's talk, Ibyang!

56
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,609
Hey!

57
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:35,655
[music fades]

58
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:36,990
Ibyang?

59
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:40,743
[Atoy] Ibyang.

60
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:45,331
[Ibyang sighs]

61
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:47,333
Ibyang, can we talk?

62
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,420
I'm going to sleep!

63
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,088
I'm tired.

64
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:56,676
- [imitates snoring sound]
- [mellow music playing]

65
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,309
Okay, okay…

66
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:08,062
I have something for you there…

67
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:10,064
Come… Come home.

68
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:12,650
You can rest at the house.

69
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,360
It'll be a waste if you don't get
what I bought for you.

70
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,321
It's your favorite.

71
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,073
Ibyang.

72
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,825
Ibyang, I'm sorry.

73
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:25,830
- The decision I made hurt me too, but…
- [sniffles]

74
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:30,335
[Atoy sighs] Please, come back home.

75
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:32,003
I shouldn't.

76
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:34,172
[sniffles]

77
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:40,553
Because… I shouldn't be in your house.

78
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,514
Janine should be the one.

79
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:47,810
Because she's your real child.

80
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:50,563
That's why you chose her.

81
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:54,025
You don't need to explain.

82
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,319
[melancholic music playing]

83
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:00,949
Okay.

84
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:04,994
I'll just send
what I got for you through Ame.

85
00:04:06,537 --> 00:04:08,456
But Ibyang, remember this.

86
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:10,166
I love you.

87
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:13,294
If you change your mind,

88
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:16,297
you're always welcome at home.

89
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,174
I'll be there, waiting for you.

90
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,260
All right?

91
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:24,681
I love you too.

92
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:27,308
[sniffles]

93
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:31,312
I just don't want your family
to have problems.

94
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:38,319
I'm not really your child.

95
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:42,782
I'm just borrowing you as a father.

96
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:16,024
[epic music playing]

97
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,336
[crying]

98
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:41,716
[music fades]

99
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:45,011
[suave theme music playing]

100
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,431
[motorcycle revving]

101
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:50,349
[sewing machine whirring]

102
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:51,309
[scratches]

103
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:52,351
[snipping]

104
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,230
[sewing machine clacking]

105
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:57,940
[gunshots]

106
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,401
[gunshots]

107
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:01,903
[clacking]

108
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,321
[clicking]

109
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:04,447
[snipping]

110
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:07,116
[music swells]

111
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,494
[electronic blipping]

112
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:13,539
[music fades]

113
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,459
[birds chirping]

114
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:17,960
Audrey, dear!

115
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:22,090
How was your vacation with your daughter?

116
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:25,718
It was fine, Dad. Janine enjoyed it.

117
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:29,972
But you… Your smile is different.

118
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,641
- [in English] What?
- [pleasant music playing]

119
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:33,309
Dad, it's nothing!

120
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:35,520
[in English] Oh, come on,
Audrey, my child.

121
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:36,437
[Audrey chuckles softly]

122
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:38,856
It's impossible that it's nothing.

123
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,566
You're smiling up to your ears.

124
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:42,360
Ah--

125
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:43,861
[in English] Dad!

126
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,029
[chuckles]

127
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:49,992
[in English] Okay, fine.

128
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:55,498
[in English] The guy
that you heard on the phone…

129
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,417
was Atoy.

130
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,753
[feel-good music playing]

131
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:04,674
[in English] We've decided to pick up
where we left off.

132
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:11,264
We agreed to fix our relationship,

133
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,891
since we have a child.

134
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:17,520
[in English] Okay.

135
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:23,609
[in English] Why don't you
invite Atoy over

136
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,028
for dinner tonight?

137
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:30,867
[in English] Are you sure, Dad?

138
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,871
[relieved chuckle]

139
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:37,623
[in English] Okay.

140
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,460
[in English] Thank you.

141
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:55,391
- [music fades]
- [Red, in English] See?

142
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,560
[Red smirks]

143
00:07:57,643 --> 00:07:58,853
Crazy, right?

144
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:01,981
[Red sighs]

145
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,110
[in English] I-Is that Atoy?

146
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,320
[in English] C-Can I see?

147
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:11,908
[suspicious music playing]

148
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,328
Was he with you on your trip?

149
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,997
[in English] Um, yes.

150
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:21,918
Daddy Atoy might even join us
here at home again.

151
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:25,630
Because he and Mommy are back together!

152
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:27,423
- [titters]
- [Martina smirks]

153
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,549
[in English] Really?

154
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,595
I mean-- I have a bad feeling
he'll just leave your mommy again.

155
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,180
She'll get hurt.

156
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:35,389
Do you want that?

157
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:38,809
Mm. Why would he leave Mommy?

158
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,312
They love each other.

159
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:43,981
[in English] You don't know that.

160
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,025
Isn't your daddy poor?

161
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:50,947
What if he only came back
because he wants to enjoy our lifestyle?

162
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:54,659
My daddy isn't that poor.

163
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:57,995
[Janine inhales] You, Aunt Martina?

164
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:01,916
Did you marry Uncle Red because he's rich?

165
00:09:01,999 --> 00:09:05,586
[laughing]

166
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:06,629
Anyway.

167
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,049
I'm just happy our family of three
is complete again.

168
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:11,759
[Janine chuckles]

169
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:15,596
[in English] That was good.
[chuckles, inhales]

170
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:17,765
[in English] This can't happen.

171
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,351
[sighs, in English] Yes.

172
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,687
This is what I was saying.

173
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:26,524
It's risky if Atoy
becomes part of our family.

174
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:29,360
You need to convince Dad to say no.

175
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,738
[in English] I know what to tell him.

176
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:36,784
[tense music playing]

177
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,121
[music fades]

178
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:43,332
[in English] Oh, yes. Uh… We're doing
something about it.

179
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:44,250
[in English] Dad.

180
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,211
[in English] I'll call you back.
Thank you.

181
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,005
[in English] Yes.

182
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,008
You need to talk to Audrey.

183
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:55,928
Tell her it's a bad idea to get
back together with Atoy.

184
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,221
[sinister music playing]

185
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,140
[smirks] Why?

186
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:00,558
What's wrong with that?

187
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:02,310
[suspicious music playing]

188
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,811
Atoy is a tracker.

189
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,397
He has many connections.

190
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:09,150
He might dig up your past businesses.

191
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,360
Your smuggling.

192
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:13,195
[in English] What do you mean?

193
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:19,076
That ivory shipment before, remember?

194
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:21,912
[in English] You told me
everything was going well.

195
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,999
Your men messed it up again!

196
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,959
It failed because of him.

197
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:30,254
I retaliated, and someone
got dragged into it.

198
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:31,631
Atoy was there.

199
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,591
There! That's him.

200
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,343
[car engine revving]

201
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:36,510
[crashes]

202
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,930
[people gasp]

203
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:42,683
What do you mean?

204
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:45,227
It doesn't matter anymore.

205
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:47,605
It's just a bad idea.

206
00:10:48,272 --> 00:10:51,901
Say it now
before I lose patience with you!

207
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,530
[music fades]

208
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:58,908
I hit-and-run Atoy's father.

209
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,201
- What?
- [tense music playing]

210
00:11:01,535 --> 00:11:03,621
You're reckless as always!

211
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:05,039
I didn't mean it!

212
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,917
[in English] You're an idiot!

213
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:10,086
Why are you only telling me this now?

214
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:13,047
I didn't know
Atoy and Audrey were connected.

215
00:11:14,548 --> 00:11:16,300
It's a bad idea, Dad.

216
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,761
Our family is doomed
if those two end up together.

217
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:23,641
[intense music playing]

218
00:11:27,895 --> 00:11:29,605
[in English] I will deal with him.

219
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:39,657
[music swells]

220
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,659
[music fades]

221
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:44,203
Whoa! Atoy!

222
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:48,666
Looking sharp.
You're dressed to the nines!

223
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:51,377
- Ah. Thanks! Do I look good?
- Yes. Wait.

224
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,130
Is this your new mission?
Pretending to be…

225
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:55,339
a corrupt politician?

226
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:57,800
Oh, take me with you.
I'll pretend to be your bodyguard.

227
00:11:57,883 --> 00:11:59,677
Like, uh…

228
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:00,761
[in English] Roger, roger.

229
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,013
- [quirky music playing]
- Ah, Congressman is coming out. Roger.

230
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,223
Congressman is coming out.

231
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:05,391
I can do it. Take me with you.

232
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:07,768
No. I'm going to Audrey's.

233
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,605
Yes, and you know them, right?
They're rich.

234
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:16,193
Of course, I want to look presentable,
even if I'm nervous.

235
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:18,654
- Wow!
- [Atoy] Huh?

236
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:20,239
Wow! You're something else.

237
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:22,324
You're sharper than a needle.

238
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:24,577
You even managed to find love again?

239
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:25,828
- [chuckles]
- Huh?

240
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:29,832
[stutters] Even while doing this, uh…
special super spy,

241
00:12:29,915 --> 00:12:32,001
slash, uh… tailor?

242
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:33,711
- Oh?
- [Emerson] Wow.

243
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,379
Take me with you.

244
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:39,884
[clicks tongue] ‘Son…
You know my job is dangerous.

245
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,343
You've seen it.

246
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:43,762
Sometimes I look for missing roosters.

247
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:48,350
- [chuckles]
- But most of the time… criminals.

248
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:55,357
So, even if I want you with me,
it's too dangerous.

249
00:12:56,317 --> 00:13:00,196
So, as much as possible,
don't talk about it.

250
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:02,573
Make sure no one knows.

251
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:05,117
That's how it should be, so we're safe.

252
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,660
- Got you!
- Oh my god! Son of a-

253
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,537
- [Kurt gasps]
- [quirky music playing]

254
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:09,997
[in English] Guys, it's just me,
Brother Kurt!

255
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,291
What are you doing there,
Brother Kurt? Huh?

256
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:13,417
What's wrong with you?
Have you been there long?

257
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:14,210
- Who sent you?
- [gasps]

258
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,336
You're a spy, aren't you?

259
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:16,420
No, no, no!

260
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:20,591
[in English] I just-- I came by
to give Atoy and Ibyang some pares

261
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,176
'cause you know, I have--

262
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:23,677
[in English] I had some extra.

263
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:26,138
And then, you know,
I heard your guys' conversation,

264
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,139
so I didn't come closer.

265
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,558
[in English] But you know, I swear,
I didn't hear you guys talking.

266
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:31,352
[in English] Okay? I just-- Promise, but…

267
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,728
You know…

268
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:37,399
Is it true, Atoy,
that you're like a secret killer spy?

269
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:39,068
[in English] Like… [chuckles] Like…

270
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,445
- "Bond. James Bond."
- [quirky sting]

271
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:44,573
Or maybe… uh… [stutters]

272
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,659
Who was that? [imitates gun firing sound]

273
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,869
[in English] Uh, John Wick or maybe even…

274
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:50,329
[imitates grunting sound]

275
00:13:50,412 --> 00:13:51,288
Jackie Chan!

276
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:52,248
Something like that.

277
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:53,582
Uh, it's, uh…

278
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:56,919
[in English] It's actually something
like that, but not something like that.

279
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:58,087
[in English] None of the above.

280
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,797
[in English] He's simply, uh…

281
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,383
Atoy, aka The Master Cutter.

282
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,387
- [laid-back music playing]
- [grunting and groaning]

283
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:10,474
[thumping and thudding]

284
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:13,769
That's why he's good at fighting!

285
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,897
Boom! Whoa!

286
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:19,692
[in English] But that's why
you have to shut your mouth,

287
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:21,735
- because nobody knows.
- [gasps]

288
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,863
[in English] Yes, yes, yes.
Of course, of course, of course!

289
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:24,780
Of course.

290
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:27,867
But Atoy, you know,
if you need my help at all,

291
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:33,080
like catering for your missions
or being your assistant,

292
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:34,707
I'm available. You just say when.

293
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,125
- Hmm.
- [Emerson cackles]

294
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,252
- [in English] Wait a minute.
- [sighs]

295
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:40,212
[in English] Brother Kurt,
you have to get in line,

296
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:42,631
because I'm the number two
of Mr. Man over here.

297
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,134
Hmm…

298
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:47,261
Brother Kurt…

299
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:49,889
[music fades]

300
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:51,223
Whatever you heard…

301
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:52,266
Hmm?

302
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,143
Nothing, nothing.

303
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:57,688
[in English] That's, uh…
That's top secret. Okay?

304
00:14:58,814 --> 00:15:01,567
[in English] So, I suggest you…
you take it to your grave.

305
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:02,484
Ay.

306
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:08,198
[in English] Because, um, I can do things,
I have done things,

307
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,533
you don't want to know.

308
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,993
[rock music playing]

309
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:13,078
- [in English] Understood?
- [mutters]

310
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:14,788
Mmm.

311
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:19,585
[in English] In short, if you spill
the beans, no more pork and beans.

312
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:21,921
Ah. [titters]

313
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:23,255
I get it, guys.

314
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:24,506
[Kurt sighs]

315
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,175
- [in English] Relax, Kurt.
- [Kurt chuckles nervously]

316
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:27,217
Relax. It's just me.

317
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:33,724
[Emerson cackling]

318
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,646
[music fades]

319
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:40,940
Ibyang, eat now!

320
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:45,069
Hmm, Atoy really knows your favorites.

321
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:46,779
Come on, eat!

322
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:49,907
It would be a waste.

323
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:52,785
[melancholic music playing]

324
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:57,122
Mmm, let him and his daughter eat that.

325
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,749
[sobs]

326
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:01,669
He chose Janine anyway.

327
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:07,216
Let them eat it.

328
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:14,348
[sobbing]

329
00:16:14,431 --> 00:16:16,350
You don't want it?

330
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,727
I'll eat it then.

331
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:23,816
Hmm! It's delicious!

332
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,819
This is so delicious!

333
00:16:26,902 --> 00:16:29,196
The sauce is perfect!

334
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:33,826
Hmm! So, so good!

335
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,119
Hmm!

336
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:37,871
I might finish it all!

337
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:42,793
Hmm! Mmm-hmm. Hmm!

338
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:48,132
So yummy. Atoy is really good!

339
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:52,845
Hmm.

340
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:53,971
It really is delicious.

341
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,974
Right? Mmm, dip it more!

342
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:06,734
Ah, come on!
You're just playing hard to get!

343
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:08,318
So? Are you and Atoy okay now?

344
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:12,072
No! Let him be!

345
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:14,324
We're not okay.

346
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,546
Mmm-hmm.

347
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:32,426
Eat some more.

348
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:34,636
Mmm?

349
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,682
[in English] He's almost here, Dad.

350
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,476
[in English] Um, I told Janine
to come down in a bit.

351
00:17:40,976 --> 00:17:43,312
- [Dmitri, in English] All right.
- [in English] Everything is ready.

352
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:44,772
[tense music playing]

353
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,066
[in English] Wow, wow!

354
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:48,942
[in English] Everyone
is looking expensive.

355
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:49,902
[Red, in English] Yes.

356
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:51,320
[in English] What's the occasion?

357
00:17:55,157 --> 00:18:00,579
[pensive music playing]

358
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:03,916
Good evening.

359
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:07,461
For you.

360
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,254
[in English] Thank you.

361
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:11,507
[in English] Perfect timing.

362
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,300
Janine is coming down too.

363
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,136
Brother Atoy, why are you here?

364
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:19,389
[Dmitri, in English] I invited him, Gavin.

365
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:21,558
[music fades]

366
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:25,062
So, I've heard you and my daughter
are back together.

367
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,107
[in English] Is that right, Atoy?

368
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,068
Yes, sir.

369
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:35,447
[in English] Let's talk
about it over dinner.

370
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:36,865
[in English] Take your seats.

371
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:40,744
Atoy…

372
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,248
Sit here.

373
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:46,083
- [tense music playing]
- Why? This is my seat, right?

374
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:48,919
He's the guest.

375
00:19:01,598 --> 00:19:05,644
Sir, just give this seat to your son.

376
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:07,437
He might throw a tantrum.

377
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:11,567
You're really provoking me, huh?

378
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:13,569
[in English] Relax.

379
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:16,738
- [music fades]
- Don't stress too much. It's just a chair.

380
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:25,747
[tense music playing]

381
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:31,461
- Uh, sir, I'll just sit beside Audrey.
- Yes.

382
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,713
Stay there. You might cry otherwise.

383
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:34,631
- What did you say?
- [Dmitri, in English] That's enough, Red.

384
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,550
[upbeat rock music playing]

385
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:38,886
Sit down.

386
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:41,263
Sit down.

387
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:43,640
[chair scraping]

388
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,903
- [music concludes]
- There!

389
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,029
Oh.

390
00:19:57,112 --> 00:19:59,781
You know, while
I was watching you earlier,

391
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,408
my lips felt like
they were about to explode!

392
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:02,993
Like they'd bleed.

393
00:20:03,076 --> 00:20:06,580
You know, T-Bak,
go buy some iced water from Eploks.

394
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:07,664
There's none here.

395
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:09,541
Huh? No way!

396
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,835
I don't want to go there! It's chaotic!

397
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:17,007
Earlier, I saw Eploks' mom
being confronted by the real wife!

398
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:18,300
- [T-Bak] Do you know why?
- [Billy] Why?

399
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:20,886
Because Eploks' mom is a mistress!

400
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:22,930
[Putoy] So, Eploks is jinxed.

401
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:27,017
That's why whenever we buy
iced water there. We always lose.

402
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,685
- Exactly.
- He's the child of a mistress.

403
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:29,895
[T-Bak] Mmm-mmm.

404
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:33,106
And I'm allergic to that,
so it's a no for me!

405
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,316
[in English] No, no, no, no!

406
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:36,401
Do you have a problem
with illegitimate children?!

407
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:37,361
[tense music playing]

408
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:38,737
What's your problem?!

409
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:42,032
My problem is your attitude!

410
00:20:42,532 --> 00:20:44,368
You think you're so high and mighty!

411
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,411
Hey! Why are you angry?

412
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:48,080
We weren't even talking about you.

413
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:54,628
[music fades]

414
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:55,879
[Dmitri] Oh, my granddaughter!

415
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:57,422
- [Dmitri] Hi!
- [Audrey] Janine.

416
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:00,092
[Janine, in English] Daddy.

417
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,135
[in English] Daddy is here.

418
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:17,776
[Dmitri] Atoy, Audrey…

419
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:21,405
[in English] I appreciate
what you're trying to do.

420
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:24,366
Family is important.

421
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:26,910
[in English] It always comes first.

422
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,954
That's really what I want too.

423
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:31,081
To rebuild the family.

424
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:35,794
Especially now that Janine is here.

425
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:39,589
I want to always be present for her.

426
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,261
I wasn't close to my father.

427
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:49,683
And when we finally reconciled,

428
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:52,686
he was gone shortly.

429
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:54,438
[suspicious music playing]

430
00:21:54,521 --> 00:21:55,605
[in English] Really?

431
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:58,066
[in English] That's… That's so sad.

432
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:02,696
How did Grandpa die, Daddy?

433
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:05,032
He was hit-and-run, child.

434
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:09,328
[Atoy] So, you, be careful
when crossing the street.

435
00:22:10,787 --> 00:22:11,830
[Dmitri] Atoy…

436
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,541
[in English] I'm sorry to hear that.

437
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:17,461
[in English] Yes, sir.

438
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:20,172
His death anniversary is coming soon.

439
00:22:21,506 --> 00:22:22,924
Imagine, until now,

440
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:28,096
I still don't know who ran him over.

441
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:34,603
We're sitting in front of food,
and we're talking about death?

442
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:36,605
It's like we're uneducated.

443
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:40,776
[sighs] Right. Sorry.

444
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:43,070
- [Audrey] Mmm.
- You're smart, huh.

445
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,405
Your tie is crooked.

446
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:46,782
[suspicious music playing]

447
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:48,492
- What's it to you--
- [Dmitri] Red!

448
00:22:49,618 --> 00:22:51,036
[in English] Just fix your tie.

449
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,248
[in English] Fix my tie!

450
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,001
- [tense music playing]
- You're not saying it.

451
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,630
[in English] Atoy, please.

452
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:14,392
[in English] Shall we?

453
00:23:17,646 --> 00:23:18,480
[in English] Yes.

454
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:25,529
[music swells]

455
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,536
[music fades]

456
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:34,538
[Dmitri, in English] Finish him, son!

457
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:39,376
[multiple gunfire]

458
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:42,629
[suspicious music playing]

459
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:48,301
Who taught you?

460
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:51,346
[in English] Yours truly!

461
00:23:58,186 --> 00:23:59,479
[in English] You wanna try it?

462
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:03,358
[Red] No need.

463
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:06,153
What did your father teach you?

464
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:09,281
To sew.

465
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:13,910
He was a master cutter, a tailor.

466
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:18,707
But because of sewing, I was trained well.

467
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:20,750
A gun is like a needle.

468
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:22,210
You can't tremble.

469
00:24:23,003 --> 00:24:25,630
It must always be precise.

470
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:29,467
Because the wrong hole ruins the fabric.

471
00:24:30,093 --> 00:24:33,138
The wrong shot ruins the target.

472
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:34,598
[suspicious music playing]

473
00:24:34,681 --> 00:24:36,349
A gun is an extension of the hand.

474
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:39,728
Like a sewing machine,
the hand is the extension of a tailor.

475
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:44,065
[in English] Firm grip, solid stance.

476
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:45,775
[gunfire blasting]

477
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:51,281
- [music swells]
- I didn't know

478
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:54,367
a tailor could become a shooter.

479
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:58,121
So, you're not just a tracker.

480
00:24:58,622 --> 00:25:00,123
You're also a marksman.

481
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:03,001
Just inspired, sir.

482
00:25:04,419 --> 00:25:07,422
And this is what I'll do to the one
who ran over my father.

483
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:10,926
[gunfire blasting]

484
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:13,887
[tense music playing]

485
00:25:38,703 --> 00:25:39,704
[music fades]

486
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:45,752
[electronic blipping]

487
00:25:50,173 --> 00:25:52,634
Just because I treated you well

488
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:54,719
doesn't mean you're the one
I want for my daughter.

489
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:56,137
I'm just being nice to you

490
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,973
because you're the father
of my grandchild…

491
00:25:58,056 --> 00:25:59,307
UP NEXT

492
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:00,642
…and that's all.

493
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:02,602
Uh, what do you mean, sir?

494
00:26:02,686 --> 00:26:06,356
[in English] Your mission
is just to retrieve information.

495
00:26:06,439 --> 00:26:07,899
What information?

496
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:11,403
A terrorist group known as Obsidian,

497
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:15,031
reportedly training now
in the Philippines.

498
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:17,742
[Mercado] This is a national
security matter, Atoy.

499
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:18,660
[Atoy, in English] <i>Hello, sir!</i>

500
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:24,499
<i>I found my brother, Andrei Sokolov.</i>

501
00:26:24,582 --> 00:26:25,583
[Samir, in English] Stop.

502
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:27,961
[in English] What is your name?

503
00:26:28,044 --> 00:26:28,920
[Kurt] <i>Sokolov.</i>

504
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:32,090
[in English] Mr. Alexei Sokolov.

505
00:26:32,173 --> 00:26:35,510
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

506
00:26:35,593 --> 00:26:37,178
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

507
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:39,723
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
